/// Synopsis: an alert and `#primary` inside a dark pill (a badge, a dark tag, the header of a table, a dark cell) are yellow where the yellow reads, a contrast of 3:1 or more with the pill (`primary`, `tertiary`, `quaternary-dark`, `neutral-dark`), and dark blue under it (`quaternary`, `neutral`, `secondary-dark`, `primary-light`). Page 1: a green badge (dark blue), the green badge of a `#tip` callout (dark blue; the alert of its body takes the color of the box), a red tag (yellow) and a green one (dark blue), both with white text, and the table header (yellow); page 2: one badge of each color, named in its box, and a green cell. Page 3: `#secondary`, `#tertiary` and `#quaternary` keep their color on a pill where it reads (3:1 or more: the yellow on the blue, the dark gray and the red) and otherwise follow the alert, yellow or dark blue; page 4: a red word in the red badge and the red `===` pill of an exercise, and in a tag of its own color; page 5: pills where the red or the green reads and keeps its color (`neutral-darkest`, `primary-dark`, `tertiary-dark`, `quaternary-darker` and a `primary-dark` cell), the expected colors written in each box, as on page 3. The header and a dark cell on the blue are also in `config/emphasis-on-blue`; the light pills, tags and cells are on page 8 of `new/light-colors`.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
